            bioParagraphs: ["Andrew came from Bethsaida, brother of Simon Peter and a fisherman like him. He was a disciple of John the Baptist and one of the two who, hearing John, followed Jesus; for this the Byzantine Church calls him \"the first called\". It was he who brought his brother to Jesus.", "In the Gospels, he is the one who points out the boy with the loaves and fish before the multiplication and who brings to Jesus the Greeks who wanted to see him. Tradition says he died crucified at Patras, in Greece, on an X-shaped cross, \"Saint Andrew's cross\"."],
